            <ArticleTitle>Retained forceps: an unusual cause of intestinal obstruction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>148-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Medical errors during surgery are usually under-reported and not well studied. During the past decade, increased interest in medical malpractice has been shown by both the public and the authorities. A particularly high risk of medical errors is seen in emergency settings, unexpected change in procedure, or in patients with a high body mass index. Visually or acoustically controlled monitoring before wound closure are recommended to eliminate human error as thoroughly as possible. Prevention remains the key to solving the problem.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
